  "title": "Nazca Lines",
  "summary": "The Nazca (Nasca) Lines are lines and figures of animals and geometric shapes made on the arid Nasca Plain in Peru by clearing the dark surface stones to expose lighter soil. Sources date them to between roughly 500 BCE and 200–500 CE; their purpose is debated, with most scientists favouring ritual explanations.",
